  ('listening-better', 218, 'When you are asked, "Are you listening?" today, tell the truth, and then start again.'),
  ('listening-better', 219, 'Ask a child what they would change about the house, the family, or the day, and listen without defending anything.'),
  ('listening-better', 220, 'Notice when someone''s voice drops or speeds up, and ask gently what just happened.'),
  ('listening-better', 221, 'Listen to a parent''s advice about your life and thank them for caring before you say anything else.'),
  ('listening-better', 222, 'Ask a coworker how their family is doing, if you know they have one, and remember the names.'),
  ('listening-better', 223, 'When a friend shares a win, ask what it took to get there.'),
  ('listening-better', 224, 'At the end of one conversation today, say, "Did I miss anything?" and mean it.'),
  ('listening-better', 225, 'Ask your partner one question you would ask on a first date, and listen like it is one.'),
  ('listening-better', 226, 'Ask a coworker what success looks like for them this quarter, and listen for what they care about beyond the numbers.'),
  ('listening-better', 227, 'When someone gives you a compliment today, hear it all the way through without deflecting.'),
  ('listening-better', 228, 'Ask your child to tell you about a dream they had, and ask what it felt like rather than what it meant.'),
  ('listening-better', 229, 'Listen to a friend talk about their family without comparing it to yours.'),
  ('listening-better', 230, 'On a spring morning, ask someone what they are hoping for this year, and let the answer take its time.'),
  ('listening-better', 231, 'When a coworker interrupts you, let them finish, then return to your point calmly. Notice how it feels to hear them first.'),
  ('listening-better', 232, 'Ask a parent what they are proud of in their own life, not in yours, and listen with fresh ears.'),
  ('listening-better', 233, 'Listen to a friend''s frustration with their partner without taking sides.'),
  ('listening-better', 234, 'When someone shares a small piece of news, treat it as if it were big, and ask about it.'),
  ('listening-better', 235, 'Ask your partner what they wish you understood about their work, and let them explain for as long as they want.'),
  ('listening-better', 236, 'Notice when you start scanning the room while someone talks. Bring your eyes back to them.'),
  ('listening-better', 237, 'Ask a coworker about a time something went wrong and what they learned, and hear the whole arc.'),
  ('listening-better', 238, 'Give a friend on the phone the same eye contact you would in person: look at nothing else.'),
  ('listening-better', 239, 'When a child says "Never mind," say, "I want to hear it," and wait patiently.'),
  ('listening-better', 240, 'Listen for what a customer or client is worried about beneath their question, and speak to that.'),
  ('listening-better', 241, 'Ask your partner about a friendship of theirs you know little about.'),
  ('listening-better', 242, 'Sit at the kitchen table after dinner and ask, "Anything else on your mind?" Then stay seated.'),
  ('listening-better', 243, 'Listen to a coworker rehearse a presentation and ask what they want feedback on before you give any.'),
  ('listening-better', 244, 'When your parent tells you how to do something you already know, hear it as care and say thank you.'),
  ('listening-better', 245, 'Notice when a friend hedges, "It''s probably nothing, but..." and say, "Tell me anyway."'),
  ('listening-better', 246, 'Ask a stranger at a dog park, a playground, or a gym one question and listen to the entire answer.'),
  ('listening-better', 247, 'When a coworker is anxious about a deadline, listen for what they need, more time, more help, or just a witness.'),
  ('listening-better', 248, 'Ask your partner what they would like more of from you, and hear it without keeping score.'),
  ('listening-better', 249, 'Let a child tell you about a video game level in full detail, and ask what makes it hard.'),
  ('listening-better', 250, 'In a disagreement over text, reread the other person''s last message before typing yours.'),
  ('listening-better', 251, 'Ask a friend what has been the hardest part of parenting, caregiving, or work lately, and just receive it.'),
  ('listening-better', 252, 'Listen to a coworker''s tone in a message today. If it seems off, ask them in person how they are.'),
  ('listening-better', 253, 'Ask an older relative about a song they loved as a teenager and why, and listen to the story behind it.'),
  ('listening-better', 254, 'When someone says "You wouldn''t understand," say, "Help me try," and keep quiet.'),
  ('listening-better', 255, 'Notice when you are waiting for a pause so you can talk. Let two pauses go by.'),
  ('listening-better', 256, 'Ask your partner to describe the moment they felt happiest this week.'),
  ('listening-better', 257, 'Listen to a friend''s account of a doctor''s visit without minimizing or catastrophizing.'),
  ('listening-better', 258, 'Find out which part of the day a coworker enjoys most, and find out why.'),
  ('listening-better', 259, 'When a child lies or exaggerates, listen for the wish underneath the story before you correct it.'),
  ('listening-better', 260, 'In the car on a long drive, ask, "What is something you have never told me?" and be ready to hear it.'),
  ('listening-better', 261, 'Ask a cashier or a barista if it has been a busy day, and stay curious about the answer.'),
  ('listening-better', 262, 'When a friend shares a decision you would never make, ask what feels right about it to them.'),
  ('listening-better', 263, 'Listen to your partner talk about their parents without offering your assessment of them.'),
  ('listening-better', 264, 'Ask a coworker how they would solve a problem you are stuck on, and listen all the way through before you judge the idea.'),
  ('listening-better', 265, 'On a hot summer night, sit outside with someone and ask what they remember about summers growing up.'),
  ('listening-better', 266, 'Notice when a conversation is really about something else, and gently ask, "Is this about the dishes, or something bigger?"'),
  ('listening-better', 267, 'Ask a child which friend they played with today and what they did, and remember the friend''s name.'),
  ('listening-better', 268, 'When someone tells you their opinion of a hard topic, try to state it back in words they would accept.'),
  ('listening-better', 269, 'Ask a friend to describe their perfect day off, and listen for what they are missing.'),
  ('listening-better', 270, 'Listen to your parent talk about their health without immediately taking over.'),
  ('listening-better', 271, 'Ask a coworker for their honest reaction to your idea, and let them finish before you defend it.'),
  ('listening-better', 272, 'When your partner is venting about their day, ask, "What was the worst moment?" and let them tell it.'),
  ('listening-better', 273, 'Listen to a teenager describe a friend drama without asking who was right.'),
  ('listening-better', 274, 'Ask a neighbor about their garden, their car, or their dog, and follow the conversation past the small talk.'),
  ('listening-better', 275, 'Catch yourself judging whether someone is right while they talk. Listen instead for what they feel.'),
  ('listening-better', 276, 'Ask a friend what they wish people asked them more often, and then ask it.'),
  ('listening-better', 277, 'When a coworker shares a personal struggle, listen first, and ask about work later.'),
  ('listening-better', 278, 'Ask your child what they think you are good at and bad at, and listen to both without arguing.'),
  ('listening-better', 279, 'Listen to someone from a different generation talk about their worries, and resist explaining how times have changed.'),
  ('listening-better', 280, 'Ask a coworker, "What am I not seeing here?" and take their answer seriously.'),
  ('listening-better', 281, 'If your partner brings up a friend''s problem, listen without solving the friend''s life.'),
  ('listening-better', 282, 'Ask an older person in your life what they miss about the way things used to be, and hear it out.'),
  ('listening-better', 283, 'Notice when a friend changes the subject quickly, and later ask gently if they wanted to say more.'),
  ('listening-better', 284, 'Ask a coworker how they prefer to be thanked, and take note.'),
  ('listening-better', 285, 'Allow a patient, a student, or a caller the time to finish their question before you begin your answer.'),
  ('listening-better', 286, 'When your child talks about a fear of the dark, a monster, or a storm, ask what would make it feel safer.'),
  ('listening-better', 287, 'Hear a friend''s whole account of a trip and ask about the moment they will remember most.'),
  ('listening-better', 288, 'Ask your partner what has been on their mind that they have not said yet, and wait for it.'),
  ('listening-better', 289, 'Try one conversation where you speak less than a third of the time.'),
  ('listening-better', 290, 'Ask a coworker about a book, a show, or a hobby they mentioned, and let them go deep.'),
  ('listening-better', 291, 'When a family member shares a health worry at a holiday table, listen and follow up later, privately.'),
  ('listening-better', 292, 'Ask a friend what they would want if money were not a problem, and listen for the values in the answer.'),
  ('listening-better', 293, 'Notice when your mind drifts to your to-do list while your partner is speaking. Say, "Sorry, say that again," and hear it.'),
  ('listening-better', 294, 'Ask a child about a book they are reading and let them tell you the plot, spoilers and all.'),
  ('listening-better', 295, 'When someone tells you about their day in one word, ask for the second word.'),
  ('listening-better', 296, 'Listen to a coworker vent about a client without adding your own gripes.'),
  ('listening-better', 297, 'Ask your parent about a friend of theirs you have heard of but never met.'),
  ('listening-better', 298, 'In a heated moment, say, "Let me make sure I understand," and repeat back their concern before you respond.'),
  ('listening-better', 299, 'Ask a friend how they really feel about a change in their life, and let them contradict themselves.'),
  ('listening-better', 300, 'Listen to someone practice a speech, a toast, or a pitch and tell them one thing that landed.'),
  ('listening-better', 301, 'Ask a coworker what they are worried about heading into a busy week, and hear it out before offering to help.'),
  ('listening-better', 302, 'When your partner shares an idea for the house, the trip, or the future, ask two questions before you mention cost or timing.'),
  ('listening-better', 303, 'Listen to a child explain why they are not tired at bedtime, and take one of their reasons seriously.'),
  ('listening-better', 304, 'Ask a friend what made them laugh this week, and let them retell the whole scene.'),
  ('listening-better', 305, 'Notice the moment you feel the urge to defend yourself in a conversation today, and ask a question instead.'),
  ('listening-better', 306, 'Ask a parent to tell you about the day you were born, or the day you arrived, and let them add every detail they want.'),
  ('listening-better', 307, 'In a meeting, write down a question you want to ask and hold it until the speaker has finished the whole thought.'),
  ('listening-better', 308, 'Ask a coworker what they would tell their younger self about this job, and listen for the lesson under the story.'),
  ('listening-better', 309, 'When someone is telling you something painful, keep your phone in your pocket even when it buzzes.'),
  ('listening-better', 310, 'Ask your partner how they would describe your week, and listen to how they saw it.'),
  ('listening-better', 311, 'Listen to a friend''s dream for their career without pointing out the obstacles.'),
  ('listening-better', 312, 'Ask a child what the best thing about their teacher is, and let the answer surprise you.'),
  ('listening-better', 313, 'On a crisp fall walk, ask someone what they want the next few months to feel like, and listen without planning.'),
  ('listening-better', 314, 'Notice when you say "Yeah, no, totally" as filler. Replace it once with a real question about what they just said.'),
  ('listening-better', 315, 'Ask a coworker how a change at work is affecting them, and listen for the part they would not say in a meeting.'),
  ('listening-better', 316, 'When a friend says "I''m being dramatic," say, "You''re not. Keep going."'),
  ('listening-better', 317, 'Find out what your partner needs to hear from you more often, and listen without explaining why you have not said it.'),
  ('listening-better', 318, 'Listen to a parent''s story about their own parents, and ask what they inherited from them.'),
  ('listening-better', 319, 'Ask a coworker whether they would rather think out loud or be asked questions, and listen the way they prefer.'),
  ('listening-better', 320, 'When a child shows you a drawing, ask them to tell you about it before you say it is nice.'),
  ('listening-better', 321, 'Ask a friend about the last time they felt truly rested, and listen to what made it possible.'),
  ('listening-better', 322, 'In a conversation with someone you find hard, count how many times you agree silently, and tell them once.'),
  ('listening-better', 323, 'Listen to your partner''s request for a change without listing what you already do.'),
  ('listening-better', 324, 'Ask a coworker for the story behind a decision that predates you, and let them tell it their way.'),
  ('listening-better', 325, 'On a lazy Sunday, ask whoever is around what they would do with an extra hour, and listen to the whole fantasy.'),
  ('listening-better', 326, 'When a friend tells you they are struggling, ask, "How long has this been going on?" and hear the whole timeline.'),
  ('listening-better', 327, 'Listen to a child''s plan for their birthday, however impossible, without saying no yet.'),
  ('listening-better', 328, 'Ask an older coworker or mentor what they wish they had been asked earlier in their career.'),
  ('listening-better', 329, 'When someone stumbles over an apology, let them finish it before you say it is okay.'),
  ('listening-better', 330, 'Ask your partner what small thing you did this week that they noticed, and let them tell you about it.'),
  ('listening-better', 331, 'Practice asking "How did that land for you?" after sharing news, and listen to the honest answer.'),
  ('listening-better', 332, 'Listen to a friend describe their home town without comparing it to yours.'),
  ('listening-better', 333, 'Ask a coworker about the part of their job nobody sees, and pay attention to how they describe it.'),
  ('listening-better', 334, 'When a child asks a big question, about death, God, or fairness, ask what they think first, and listen fully.'),
  ('listening-better', 335, 'Ask a parent what they worry about for themselves, not for you, and stay with the answer.'),
  ('listening-better', 336, 'Listen to a customer or client''s frustration without explaining company policy first.'),
  ('listening-better', 337, 'Ask a friend how their body is feeling these days, and listen without prescribing anything.'),
  ('listening-better', 338, 'When your partner describes a conversation with their boss, ask how it felt rather than what they should have said.'),
  ('listening-better', 339, 'Let a coworker finish explaining a bug, a problem, or a complaint before you offer your theory.'),
  ('listening-better', 340, 'Ask a neighbor what they like most about living here, and let them tell you why they stay.'),
  ('listening-better', 341, 'Listen to a teenager''s music in the car and ask what they like about it.'),
  ('listening-better', 342, 'Ask a friend about something they are afraid to hope for, and make it safe to say.'),
  ('listening-better', 343, 'When your child says "You don''t get it," say, "You''re right, I might not. Explain it to me."'),
  ('listening-better', 344, 'Ask a coworker what the last week has been like at home, if you know them well enough, and just listen.'),
  ('listening-better', 345, 'Sit on the porch or the steps on the last warm evening of the year with someone and ask what they will remember from this year.'),
  ('listening-better', 346, 'Let your partner tell you about a coworker or friend you have never met, and ask enough questions to picture them.'),
  ('listening-better', 347, 'Ask a family member about a tradition they would like to start, and take the idea seriously.'),
  ('listening-better', 348, 'When a stranger strikes up a conversation in line, listen to them for the whole wait instead of nodding politely.'),
  ('listening-better', 349, 'Find out what question a friend would love to be asked at a party, and ask it.'),
  ('listening-better', 350, 'Notice when you are storing up your response while someone talks. Empty your hands, and hear the rest.'),
  ('listening-better', 351, 'Ask your parent what their favorite memory of you as a child is, and let them tell it slowly.'),
  ('listening-better', 352, 'Listen to a coworker describe how they see a conflict on the team, and repeat their view back before you share yours.'),
  ('listening-better', 353, 'When your partner says, "Never mind, it''s not important," say, "It is to me," and wait.'),
  ('listening-better', 354, 'Ask a child where grown-ups get things wrong, and let them make their whole case.'),
  ('listening-better', 355, 'Listen to a friend recount a fight with a family member without deciding who was right.'),
  ('listening-better', 356, 'Ask a coworker to describe their ideal work day, and remember one thing you could help with.'),
  ('listening-better', 357, 'When you reread an old text thread today, notice where you missed what the other person was saying.'),
  ('listening-better', 358, 'Ask your partner about a belief of theirs that has changed over time, and listen to the journey.'),
  ('listening-better', 359, 'Listen to a family member describe the holidays they remember from childhood, and ask what they miss about them.'),
  ('listening-better', 360, 'Invite a friend to name something they are proud of that nobody has noticed yet, and be the one who notices.'),
  ('listening-better', 361, 'When you notice you are half-listening on a call tonight, tell the person, "Say that once more, I want to get it right."'),
  ('listening-better', 362, 'Ask a child which things they would like to do more of together, and listen without checking the calendar.'),
  ('listening-better', 363, 'Listen to someone tell you about their faith, their doubt, or their questions without steering them anywhere.'),
  ('listening-better', 364, 'Ask your partner, at the end of the day, "What did I not ask you about that you wish I had?"'),
  ('listening-better', 365, 'Write down one thing you heard today that changed your mind, even slightly, and tell the person who said it.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 1, 'Step outside for two minutes this morning before you check anything on a screen. Notice the temperature of the air on your face.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 2, 'Find a patch of sky from wherever you are and watch one cloud until it changes shape or drifts out of view.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 3, 'Take your first sip of coffee or tea standing outside your door today, even if it is only for that sip.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 4, 'Walk to the nearest tree and put your palm flat on its bark for ten slow breaths.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 5, 'Eat lunch outside today, on a bench, a step, a curb, or the tailgate of a car, and stay for the whole meal.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 6, 'Stand outside at dusk tonight and watch for the moment the streetlights flicker on.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 7, 'Open your front door, stand on the threshold, and take five deep breaths of outdoor air before you start your day.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 8, 'Spend five minutes outside at lunch with your back to the building and your face toward the light.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 9, 'Go outside and find something green, a weed in a sidewalk crack counts, and look at it closely for one minute.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 10, 'Listen outside for one full minute tonight and count how many different sounds you can pick out.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 11, 'Take a photo of the sky from the same spot you will use again tomorrow, and see how different it looks.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 12, 'Stand in the rain for thirty seconds today with your hood up, and notice the sound it makes around you.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 13, 'Walk to the end of your block and back before dinner, looking only at what is above the rooflines.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 14, 'Sit on your front step, stoop, or balcony for ten minutes this evening with nothing in your hands.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 15, 'Step outside on a cold morning, dress for it, and watch your breath turn to mist for one minute.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 16, 'Find the warmest sunny spot near your building and stand in it for five minutes on your break.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 17, 'Notice which direction the wind is coming from today by turning slowly until you feel it on your face.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 18, 'Take the long way from the car, bus, or train to your door, adding at least two minutes outdoors.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 19, 'Look for the first sign of the season changing, a bud, a red leaf, a bare branch, a crocus, and name it out loud.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 20, 'Bring a chair, a cushion, or a folded towel outside and sit on it for ten minutes wherever there is room.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 21, 'Go outside after dark and find the brightest star or planet you can see through the light around you.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 22, 'Walk once around the outside of your building or block at midday and notice what the light does to the walls.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 23, 'Stand under a tree in the rain if it is safe and listen to how the drops sound different on the leaves.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 24, 'Take a phone call outside today instead of at your desk, and keep walking slowly while you talk.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 25, 'Look up from a parking lot for one minute and notice how much sky there is above the cars.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 26, 'Open a window wide for five minutes this morning and lean out into the air, or step outside if you can.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 27, 'Go out at sunrise this weekend, or as close to it as you can manage, and watch the color arrive.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 28, 'Find a body of water near you, a pond, a creek, a fountain, a puddle, and watch its surface for two minutes.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 29, 'Stand outside in the summer heat for one minute in the shade, and notice how the air feels different there.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 30, 'Take your evening snack or drink outside and eat it slowly while the light fades.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 31, 'Notice three smells on your way to the mailbox, the bus stop, or the car today, and name them.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 32, 'Step outside during a work break and stretch your gaze to the farthest point you can see.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 33, 'Sit outside while the sky is still light this evening and notice how long the light lasts at this time of year.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 34, 'Walk barefoot on grass, sand, or a clean patch of ground for one minute, if it is safe and warm enough.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 35, 'Stand on a corner near home and watch the sky in all four directions before you go back in.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 36, 'Find a bench you have never sat on and sit there for five minutes today.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 37, 'Look at a tree you pass every day and count how many colors are in its leaves or bark.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 38, 'Step outside first thing and check the weather with your skin instead of an app.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 39, 'Walk to a nearby park or green space at lunch, even if you only stay for three minutes once you arrive.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 40, 'Bundle up and stand outside at night in winter to see how the cold changes the sound of the street.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 41, 'Stand outside with your eyes closed for one minute and notice what you can feel on your skin: sun, wind, mist, cold.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 42, 'Watch birds from outside your door for five minutes and count how many kinds you see or hear.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 43, 'Take your morning stretch, or your first yawn, outside on the step instead of in the kitchen.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 44, 'Notice the exact moment you step from indoor air to outdoor air today, and pause there for three breaths.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 45, 'Hang around outside a little longer after taking out the trash or recycling tonight, and look up.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 46, 'Find some shade on a hot afternoon and sit in it for ten minutes with a cold drink.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 47, 'Go outside the moment it stops raining and smell the air.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 48, 'Walk under the trees along your street and notice where the leaves are thickest and where the light gets through.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 49, 'Stand at a bus stop, a crosswalk, or a corner and watch the sky instead of your phone while you wait.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 50, 'Take a slow lap of a parking lot at lunch and find one living thing growing there.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 51, 'Watch the sunset from a spot you have never watched it from before.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 52, 'Go outside for five minutes at the same time tomorrow that you went out today, and see what has changed.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 53, 'Notice the smell of a neighbor''s dinner, a laundromat, cut grass, or wet pavement as you walk outside this evening.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 54, 'Sit under a porch, awning, or overhang during a rain shower and watch the water fall from the edge.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 55, 'Step out onto a balcony, fire escape landing, or doorstep after midnight if you are awake, and breathe the quiet.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 56, 'Look for the moon during the daytime today. It is often up and easy to miss.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 57, 'Walk on the sunny side of the street this morning on purpose.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 58, 'Walk on the shady side of the street this afternoon on purpose.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 59, 'Find a place outside where you can hear water, a fountain, a drain, a stream, and listen for two minutes.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 60, 'Take five minutes outside between two meetings or tasks today, and let that be the whole point.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 61, 'Stand outside on a windy day and watch how the trees, flags, or wires move.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 62, 'Let the first snowflakes of the season land on your sleeve and look at them before they melt.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 63, 'Go outside on the shortest afternoon of winter and catch whatever daylight is left before it goes.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 64, 'Watch fog, mist, or haze from your doorstep if there is any this morning, and notice what it hides and reveals.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 65, 'Sit outside for the length of one cup of tea, however long that takes.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 66, 'Walk to a corner store, mailbox, or bus shelter instead of driving, if it is close enough and safe.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 67, 'Stand under the open sky for one minute today and simply notice that there is no ceiling.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 68, 'Notice the sound your shoes make on wet pavement, dry leaves, gravel, or snow as you walk outside.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 69, 'Spend the first five minutes of your lunch break outside, before you eat anything.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 70, 'Look for one flower blooming today, in a yard, a planter, a median, or a crack, and stop for a moment beside it.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 71, 'Find the spot near your home where the sky is widest, and go there for a few minutes this evening.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 72, 'Step outside to say goodbye to the day as the light goes, even if it is only from the doorway.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 73, 'Rest your eyes on distant trees or a far skyline for two minutes today, letting them relax after screens.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 74, 'Sit on the ground outside for a few minutes, a step, a curb, a patch of grass, and feel how solid it is.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 75, 'Open every window you can for ten minutes this morning and let the outside come in while you get ready.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 76, 'Invite someone to stand outside with you for five minutes today, a neighbor, a coworker, a kid, and talk about nothing in particular.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 77, 'Go outside on a spring morning and find the tree closest to blooming on your street.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 78, 'Take an umbrella and walk to the end of the block in the rain, noticing how the puddles hold the sky.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 79, 'Sit on a park bench in the fall and watch leaves come down for five minutes without counting them.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 80, 'Check the sky before bed tonight from outside your door, and notice whether it is clear, cloudy, or somewhere in between.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 81, 'Find a sunny wall on a cool day and lean your back against it for a few minutes to feel the stored warmth.'),
