  ('getting-outside-every-day', 294, 'Spend a few minutes outside on the first cold morning of fall and notice the smell of the air changing.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 295, 'Look at the ground after a rain and notice worms, snails, or the pattern of water in the dirt.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 296, 'Sit outside with a cup of soup or something warm on a raw gray day and eat it with the weather.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 297, 'Find a spot outdoors to watch the traffic of the sky: planes, birds, clouds, contrails.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 298, 'Pause on a pedestrian bridge, a crosswalk island, or a corner and notice the air moving through it.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 299, 'Step outside on a cloudless night in winter, dressed for it, and find the brightest constellation you can.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 300, 'Stand outside on a spring evening and listen for frogs, crickets, or peepers if you live near water or a wet field.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 301, 'Look at your street from the far end of it this evening, as if you were arriving for the first time.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 302, 'Notice the sound of your own footsteps outdoors today and how it changes on each surface.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 303, 'Go outside on a bright winter day and feel how warm the sun can be even when the air is cold.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 304, 'Find a place where you can see rain falling against a dark background, a tree, a wall, and watch for one minute.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 305, 'Spend the length of a kettle boiling outside, and come back in when it whistles or clicks off.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 306, 'Look for the last leaf clinging to a tree in late fall, and check on it again tomorrow.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 307, 'Sit in the shade of a building at noon on a hot day and watch the heat shimmer on the road.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 308, 'Take a walk in the first snow of the year, dressed for it, and notice how the sounds soften.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 309, 'Stand outside and watch a cloud''s shadow move across the ground or a building.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 310, 'Notice which birds you can hear outside your door this morning, even if you cannot name them.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 311, 'Find a tree that is budding and touch one bud gently to feel how tight it is before it opens.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 312, 'Take a break from a long screen session by standing outside and looking at the farthest thing you can see for two minutes.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 313, 'Sit outside in the wind and notice the sound it makes against your ears, your collar, your hair.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 314, 'Watch a sunrise from a parking garage roof, a hill, or your own step, whichever you can reach.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 315, 'Notice how the daylight feels on your skin at midday compared with early morning today.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 316, 'Spend your commute wait, at a stop, a platform, a curb, watching the sky instead of a screen for its whole length.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 317, 'Walk under a row of street trees and notice how the air cools as you enter their shade.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 318, 'Go outside after the first hard frost and look at what the cold did to the plants overnight.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 319, 'Notice the exact color of the sky at noon today and describe it to someone.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 320, 'Stand under a big sky at dusk on a summer evening and watch the swallows or bats begin their evening hunt.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 321, 'Find the nearest water you can dip a hand in, a fountain, a creek, a lake edge, and feel its temperature.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 322, 'Go outside while a light snow is falling and try to catch one flake on a dark glove or sleeve.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 323, 'Sit outside at the end of a long day and let your eyes rest on something green for five minutes.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 324, 'Notice how many shades of gray there are in an overcast sky today, and pick the one you like best.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 325, 'Take five slow steps outside your door this morning and stop, breathe, look, listen before you go on.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 326, 'Watch the sun set behind buildings, hills, or trees and notice the last spot it lights up.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 327, 'Step outside during a heat wave only in the early morning or evening, and notice the difference between the two.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 328, 'Stand in a light spring rain without an umbrella for one minute and let it land on your face.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 329, 'Look for a plant in a sidewalk crack, a gutter, or a rooftop and notice how it found a way to grow.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 330, 'Notice the air in a park, a lot, and a side street on the same day and see which one feels best.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 331, 'Sit outside on a summer night until you feel the first coolness arrive.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 332, 'Find one bright leaf on the ground in the fall and hold it up against the sky.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 333, 'Stand outside after a rainstorm and listen to the dripping from roofs and trees slow down.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 334, 'Go out when the wind is strong enough to hear, dress for it, and stand where it can reach you for one minute.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 335, 'Watch the morning fog lift off a field, a river, or a parking lot, if there is any where you live.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 336, 'Notice a smell outside that reminds you of being young, and stop with it for a moment.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 337, 'Look up at the streetlights coming on and count how long it takes for the whole block to light.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 338, 'Sit outside on a chilly morning with a hot drink and notice when the cold reaches your fingers.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 339, 'Stand in your yard, if you have one, or on the nearest patch of ground, and notice the sounds of the neighbors'' evening.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 340, 'Find the brightest patch of sunlight outside your building and stand in it until you feel warm.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 341, 'Take a look at the sky from wherever you are before you eat each meal today, going outside if you can.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 342, 'Walk to a place where you can hear running water and stand there for two minutes.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 343, 'Notice the different colors of the sky in the east and the west at sunset today.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 344, 'Sit on a step at dusk in the fall and watch the dark come earlier than it did last month.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 345, 'Stand outside with a friend and look at the moon together, in person or on the phone in two places.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 346, 'Notice how a hot wind, a cold wind, and a damp wind each feel different on your face across the year.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 347, 'Look for the first robins, geese, or other returning birds of spring near you.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 348, 'Spend five minutes outside without knowing what time it is, and guess when you come back in.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 349, 'Find a sunny curb or wall on a cold day and sit on it for the length of one slow drink.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 350, 'Take your outdoor moment today in complete stillness: no walking, no talking, just standing.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 351, 'Sit outside while a summer storm rumbles far away and go in when it comes near.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 352, 'Notice the shadows growing long on a fall afternoon and stand in one for a minute.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 353, 'Step outside as the last light of a winter afternoon goes and watch the sky turn from gray to navy.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 354, 'Look at the way water pools on a leaf, a car hood, or a picnic table after rain outdoors today.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 355, 'Spend one outdoor minute today on each of your senses: seeing, hearing, smelling, feeling, and tasting the air.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 356, 'Watch the sky for shooting stars on a clear late summer night, if it is dark enough where you live.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 357, 'Sit outside with someone who is quiet company and share the sky without needing to talk.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 358, 'Go outside in a snow flurry and notice how the flakes look different against the sky and against the ground.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 359, 'Stand outside on a warm spring evening and notice how the light lasts longer than it did a month ago.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 360, 'Find the shadiest tree nearby on the hottest day of the year and sit under it for ten minutes.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 361, 'Notice when the cicadas, crickets, or frogs start each evening this week and step outside to listen.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 362, 'Step out on a rainy fall morning and notice the smell of wet leaves.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 363, 'Watch the shape of the moon change over a week by stepping outside each night, clouds permitting.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 364, 'Sit outside on a bench with your eyes open and count ten things that are moving.'),
  ('getting-outside-every-day', 365, 'Give thanks to the day out loud or in your head while standing outside at dusk, and go in.')
